{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer","id":1202375,"title":"Why be a Lunar Sorcerer?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-02T17:49:40-07:00","id":1202375,"title":"Why be a Lunar Sorcerer?","content":"This is something that has been on my mind recently. 3rd edition is moving away from Lunars as &quot;basically werewolves&quot; into a bigger group of, well, Primal Heroes I guess. Shape Changers, Forest Witches, etc. But since only Solars can access the highest tier of Sorcery, what benefits do Lunars get that differentiate them?<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm NOT asking &quot;why would you make a Lunar Sorcerer&quot;, because people have all kinds of reasons to play characters they like, rather, my question is &quot;What advantages do Lunars get when learning Sorcery&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T17:51:07-07:00","id":1202376,"title":"","content":"Lunars, like anybody, get the advantage of being able to do stuff outside their native Charms.<br /> <br /> It truly doesn't matter that I'll never achieve the Solar circle, because I don't have to do that to be a world-shaking badass (and besides, until the Solar hits Essence 5, he is just as limited to the Sapphire Circle as I am)!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-02-2018, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:12:05-07:00","id":1202382,"title":"","content":"Turning Alucard's words into an analogy: Why would you learn to shoot, since you will obviously never shoot as well as the world class marksmen?<br /> Why bother singing, since you'll never reach the heights Freddy Mercury hit?<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorcery is sorcery. Stopping a bloody battle stirred by a civil war in <b>seconds</b> of effort is a mighty feat all on its own, even though it's just celestial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-02-2018, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:24:30-07:00","id":1202387,"title":"","content":"I would think Lunars would take to sorcery quite well. Its multi purpose and utility alone make it worthwhile. I do not see why they wouldn't go after sorcery and less then a Dragon blooded would which is even more limited. I started playing just last year and so far I can easily say sorcery is one of the aspects of the game I am in I love the most. I don't think any splat would need a particular advantage given to them to make it cool or more worthwhile to take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:27:22-07:00","id":1202388,"title":"","content":"I also don't feel that someone <i>has</i> to have a unique gimmick on a thing, to be valuable for having that thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:29:41-07:00","id":1202390,"title":"","content":"Plus workings mean you can replicate a lot of the feats of Solar Sorcery it just becomes more difficult than it would be for a Solar exalt. I mean death ray is great, but when it comes down to it sometimes all you really want is a lot of dead people and that can be replicated in so many glorious ways when you aren't limited to mundane weapons.*<br /> <br /> *Though you will need necromancy if you want lots of dead people courtesy of lots of hungry dead people. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:50:42-07:00","id":1202395,"title":"","content":"Celestial Circle Spells are harder to Distort, and workings of that level are harder to counter.<br /> <br /> Initiation into Celestial Circle Sorcery allows one to perform Celestial Circle sorcerous workings without the penalties of reaching beyond one's power, and reduces the penalty for attempting sorcerous workings of the Solar Circle.<br /> <br /> The primary opponents of the Lunar Exalted are the Terrestrial Exalted, who do not have these benefits.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted have great need for as much power as they can carry around with them without needing to leave behind. Sorcery certainly fits that bill. Sorcery also allows for the quick creation of valuable infrastructure which you can afford to leave behind or else destroy to deny to someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T20:39:51-07:00","id":1202426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202395#post1202395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial Circle Spells are harder to Distort, and workings of that level are harder to counter.<br /> <br /> Initiation into Celestial Circle Sorcery allows one to perform Celestial Circle sorcerous workings without the penalties of reaching beyond one's power, and reduces the penalty for attempting sorcerous workings of the Solar Circle.<br /> <br /> <b>The primary opponents of the Lunar Exalted are the Terrestrial Exalted, who do not have these benefits.</b><br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted have great need for as much power as they can carry around with them without needing to leave behind. Sorcery certainly fits that bill. Sorcery also allows for the quick creation of valuable infrastructure which you can afford to leave behind or else destroy to deny to someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bolded point cannot be overstated I think. Dragon Blooded are limited to Terrestrial Circle spells, which means they'll have a much harder time countering or distorting a Celestial Circle spell. And Celestial Circle spells can destroy armies or cities if not stopped, which, when a Wyld Hunt might send an army after you, gives you a way to easily level the playing field. Especially if you've summoned Octavian to be your bodyguard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T01:16:47-07:00","id":1202486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer#post1202375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I'm NOT asking &quot;why would you make a Lunar Sorcerer&quot;, because people have all kinds of reasons to play characters they like, rather, my question is <b>&quot;What advantages do Lunars get when learning Sorcery&quot;.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So far, the advantage is &quot;Dragon Blooded are held back even more, so it works out&quot;. But that means there's nothing a Lunar will do better than a Solar when it comes to Sorcery? They don't get to dip into Necromancy or maybe get access to a special Lunar way to gain Sorcery Motes? I ask because it seems like 3rd wants to push the &quot;witch&quot; angle a little harder but it seems like Lunars are stuck playing second fiddle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T01:25:53-07:00","id":1202488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202486#post1202486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, the advantage is &quot;Dragon Blooded are held back even more, so it works out&quot;. But that means there's nothing a Lunar will do better than a Solar when it comes to Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they, though? Why <i>must</i> your capacity for excellence be expressed through technical widgets, as opposed to, y'know, <i>doing stuff</i> that makes people recognize you as the better sorcerer?<br /> <br /> I don't intend for my most recent character to advance beyond the Terrestrial circle of sorcery for a good long while, but I expect that long before that, he's going to have quite the reputation as an awe-inspiring worker of the mystic arts, because he's gonna go out and <i>get things done</i>.<br /> <br /> As long as _____ players are fixated on having some Charm for being better _____s than everyone else, they're not actually going to be. That honor's going to go to the one who changes the face of the world with the _____ they have.<br /> <br /> (Last but not least, a propensity for &quot;witchiness&quot; doesn't have to come from or with directly enhancing sorcery. You could, for instance, get Phantom-Conjuring Performance as a Solar, and have the &quot;witchy&quot; thing locked down perfectly, weaving smoke into shapes to visually enhance the &quot;fortunes&quot; you tell in your hut in the woods or whatever\u2026 all without touching sorcery.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-03-2018, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T01:42:37-07:00","id":1202492,"title":"","content":"That's a fair read of the situation and I appreciate it, though I will be personally disappointed if there isn't something unique to the Lunar experience. Just for example, the artwork for White Reaper shows a Lunar in War Form- that's cool. That's a unique Lunar thing. I want more of that kind of mechanical diversity for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T01:45:31-07:00","id":1202494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202492#post1202492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair read of the situation and I appreciate it, though I will be personally disappointed if there isn't something unique to the Lunar experience. Just for example, the artwork for White Reaper shows a Lunar in War Form- that's cool. That's a unique Lunar thing. I want more of that kind of mechanical diversity for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, wait, in a martial arts style that <i>doesn't even mention Lunars</i>, let alone give them some greater aptitude for it than Solars, <i>an illustration of a Lunar</i> leads you to believe that you need mechanical diversity to be cool and unique?<br /> <br /> I am so confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-03-2018, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T02:35:27-07:00","id":1202507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202486#post1202486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So far, the advantage is &quot;Dragon Blooded are held back even more, so it works out&quot;. But that means there's nothing a Lunar will do better than a Solar when it comes to Sorcery? They don't get to dip into Necromancy or maybe get access to a special Lunar way to gain Sorcery Motes? I ask because it seems like 3rd wants to push the &quot;witch&quot; angle a little harder but it seems like Lunars are stuck playing second fiddle.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair we don't know a lot about Lunars for this edition, so for all we know lunars will be able to acquire multiple shaping rituals more easily even with their limitation or something we just don't know about. Solars are the god-emperor monsters who just get mastery of whatever they end up dedicating themselves to. I mean DBs are the other exalt with artifact use as an explicit part of their theme and purview this manifests as being resonant with Jade, and neutral with anything not soulsteel. By contrast solars are resonant with any artifact they don't find a way to explicitly cheese off enough to become dissonant with. <br /> <br /> Have some faith we haven't seen a lot of what Lunars are and how they're capable. Afterall Lunars are shapeshifters, with resistance nigh on immunity to wandering in the Wyld. I'd imagine that opens some possibilities when one wants to delve into sorcerery that others might not have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T03:35:24-07:00","id":1202511,"title":"","content":"Oooh. Lunar Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Mmm. While there is a power gradient between the three circles, it's worth remembering that it's kinda one of scope as much as raw energy. Terrestrial Circle spells have very immediate, direct effects. It's practical magic: useful, versatile, but no one spell of that circle is going to entirely decide a battle or rewrite the history books. Celestial Sorcery is where those big, major effects come into play. Cantata of Empty Voices in the original tale of the Bulls war against the Linowan was used by Sidereals to destroy an entire city. Second Circle Demons are beings of immense power in their own right, and Lunars can bind them. It's powerful stuff. While the Solar Circle is more powerful, Celestial Sorcery alone is significant and can do big things in the setting.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Let the Shiny Jerks have their precious god mode toys. Celestial is fine and cool in its own right, and you should underestimate a Lunar Sorcerer at your peril.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T03:37:00-07:00","id":1202514,"title":"","content":"A Lunar probably isn't learning sorcery with a motivation to be the very best, like no one ever was. They're probably learning it because they want to do things like summon demons, or teleport. Many of those things probably complement the goals and methods of Lunars very effectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I will be personally disappointed if there isn't something unique to the Lunar experience</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bThere are a few things that we already know of that are unique to the Lunar experience, some of which based on their place in the world, some of which in their psychology/Essence Fever, and some of which in mechanics such as Charms enhanced by assuming particular shapes.<br /> <br /> \u200bThey probably won't have a form of power that nobody else can really achieve or approximate, but the manner of approximation dilutes how much it feels like a Lunar.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T05:52:53-07:00","id":1202536,"title":"","content":"Well in most campaigns this won't even be a factor since Solars and Abyssals will only get their super powerful stuff at essence 5. I mean my group is playing for over a year straight and we are still not at 5 essence (although we are not the most fast progressing group I must admit). Before that, they only have their excellencies and their native charms which might give them a slight edge. <br /> <br /> Also, sorcery gives unparalleled versatility and access to effects outside the purview of one's charm suit, which is always a huge boon.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, they still can attempt solar workings which is where the real power is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:56:15-07:00","id":1202584,"title":"","content":"One might as well ask why a Dragon-Blood would bother being a sorcerer. Especially when the Realm despises sorcery. Yet they have a school that teaches it.<br /> <br /> Why do Dragon-Blooded bother learning Martial Arts? Well, the five Immaculate Styles which synergize with their Elemental Auras helps, but Martial Arts are useful even beyond that.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted can\u2019t attain Mastery effects with Martial Arts, but they get Deadly Beastmen Transformation, and may possibly get to combo their Attribute Charms with MA Charms. <br /> <br /> I would be surprised and disappointed if Dragon-Blooded don\u2019t get Essence 3 and Essence 5 Charms following Terrestrial Circle Initiation which allow them to learn other Shaping Rituals and further enhance or interact with elemental spells.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Lunar Exalted might get an Essence 5 Charm which helps with transformative spells and workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:07:24-07:00","id":1202593,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm sure that sorcery, with its widescale effects would be pretty useful for Lunars who are usually not in the most..... urban areas of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:12:28-07:00","id":1202598,"title":"","content":"Because Magma Kraken don\u2019t give a FUCK what color the shiny thing on your forehead is :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:12:05-07:00","id":1202614,"title":"","content":"Well, Celestial Circle Sorcery is pretty badass on itself, Solars are far from common, Sidereals even less so, we don't know if either Abyssals or Infernals access Solar Circle spells (possibly not), so for most matters one might as well call it Lunar Circle, because they are the guys and gals people will see trumping whole circles of DB or mortal sorcerers nine times out of ten.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ohhh, you think you are mighty because one day in the elusive future you might get the capacity to access ultra-badass spells nearly nobody has seen since the turning of the ages? Guess what this big badass ball of fur, scales, furies and insanity has a few ages of tricks hidden in its metaphorical shimmering sleeves to show off, some of which it got from surviving the terrible things your oh, so glorious golden precursor of puisant might was <b>not</b> able to. Survive, grow up and <b>then</b> let's see if i actually care.&quot;<br /> <br /> (As an aside, wasn't there in the Antagonists section a Lunar Sorcerer with a charm that let it harvest the motes of a discarded form into a spell? I'm pretty sure i saw something like that somewhere)<br /> <br /> On the matter of doing &quot;with a Lunar vibe&quot; for Sorcery, i would probably try to mine lunar hearthstones and moonsilver artifacts evocations, along with the &quot;Scarred by Nightmares&quot; initiation, for inspiration in stuff to tweak or upgrade shaping, control spells &amp; etc with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-03-2018, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:33:40-07:00","id":1202645,"title":"","content":"So you can convince your Storyteller to let you hunt and eat the heart's blood of the gods of each of the Solar Circle Spells. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:59:11-07:00","id":1202651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer#post1202375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I'm NOT asking &quot;why would you make a Lunar Sorcerer&quot;, because people have all kinds of reasons to play characters they like, rather, my question is &quot;What advantages do Lunars get when learning Sorcery&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elder Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:26:59-07:00","id":1202708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202645#post1202645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can convince your Storyteller to let you hunt and eat the heart's blood of the gods of each of the Solar Circle Spells. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh God, was there ever an idea that individual spells had their own spirits?<br /> <br /> \u200bJesus that shit got out of hand. I mean, even if there wasn't, I know there were gods of each level of martial arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:02:46-07:00","id":1202725,"title":"","content":"You can use it to summon an almost unlimited number of powerful servants/snacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:29:58-07:00","id":1202737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202708#post1202708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh God, was there ever an idea that individual spells had their own spirits?<br /> <br /> \u200bJesus that shit got out of hand. I mean, even if there wasn't, I know there were gods of each level of martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, traditionally each bowl of rice has 7 gods... but yes, let's not go there again. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow, apparently Dragonblood get some charms that help sorcery (which would be difficult to balance against Solar spells). Maybe Lunars do too.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I don't think it's necessary for each splat to have a unique advantage in sorcery. Each splat has unique advantages and disadvantages... but Martial Arts and Sorcery let you cover your holes. So a Lunar sorcerer has all the advantages of being a Lunar, but can also do things that are outside the Lunar wheelhouse, like mass ranged destruction (something DBs can do a bit, but Lunars can't), summon artefact weapons and armour (something Alchemicals can do, but Lunars can't... well, not armour anyway, maybe they can summon artefact claws), acquire/create powerful magical servants (something Sidereals can do a bit, and Dragonblood via the old-fashioned method of having kids and waiting 20 years), etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-03-2018, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:57:11-07:00","id":1202749,"title":"","content":"In short, the advantage a Lunar gets to being a sorceror is &quot;you get to do sorcery&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm... not entirely sure why that's not good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:05:23-07:00","id":1202754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202708#post1202708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh God, was there ever an idea that individual spells had their own spirits?<br /> <br /> \u200bJesus that shit got out of hand. I mean, even if there wasn't, I know there were gods of each level of martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure of that - the most correlation between MA and spirits i can remember is the animal styles and the Arguments of Virtue styles being created by exalts inspired in their observations of certain patterns of specific deitis. Ah, Mara's &amp; Five Days Darkness' relations to Black Claw &amp; Ebon Shadow styles, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:20:36-07:00","id":1202788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer#post1202375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that has been on my mind recently. 3rd edition is moving away from Lunars as &quot;basically werewolves&quot; into a bigger group of, well, Primal Heroes I guess. Shape Changers, Forest Witches, etc. But since only Solars can access the highest tier of Sorcery, what benefits do Lunars get that differentiate them?<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm NOT asking &quot;why would you make a Lunar Sorcerer&quot;, because people have all kinds of reasons to play characters they like, rather, my question is &quot;What advantages do Lunars get when learning Sorcery&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFirst I don't generally choose Sorcery to differentiate my Lunar from a Solar. Its more of a common toolbox open to just about anyone with a need and the aptitude to use it. Uniqueness is the province of native charmsets. <br /> <br /> \u200bSecondly I don't justify a Lunar's need for Sorcery based on what Solars can do. Lunars may not reach the pinnacles of Solar Circle but Terrestrial and Celestial Circles are extremely useful on their own merits. Hell...most of your sorcerer's doings are going to involve the lower tiers anyway, regardless if you are a Solar or Lunar. To the extent this matters Lunars are entirely as capable as any Solar sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:21:51-07:00","id":1202813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202708#post1202708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh God, was there ever an idea that individual spells had their own spirits?<br /> <br /> \u200bJesus that shit got out of hand. I mean, even if there wasn't, I know there were gods of each level of martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of hand, maybe.<br /> <br /> But if I were storytelling for a Lunar who wanted to defeat a Solar Sorcerer, that's a story possibility I'd bring up. Discover what spells he's got, hunt down the gods of the spells and eat them.<br /> <br /> Or bully them into taking a sabbatical, which might be easier after you eat the first one.<br /> <br /> And to be specific, this would be a story possibility because it's specifically something Lunars would/could/should (at least up to 2E) do. Other splats would have to splat at the problem differsplatingly. A Sidereal might arrange for the spell's god to be audited or to be awarded a sabbatical for excellent service.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It probably wouldn't be automatic after that, even so, but I'd count it as a heavily stacked counterspelling effort that's scaled on-par because of the story involvement.<br /> <br /> In any case, it's a pretty high-Essence, world-shaking, world-eating level of story idea anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 04-03-2018, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:58:48-07:00","id":1202819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202494#post1202494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, wait, in a martial arts style that <i>doesn't even mention Lunars</i>, let alone give them some greater aptitude for it than Solars, <i>an illustration of a Lunar</i> leads you to believe that you need mechanical diversity to be cool and unique?<br /> <br /> I am so confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like you're being deliberately obtuse. War forms give lunars bonuses to their stats, and it's canon that it combines with martial arts (as shown in the picture). Therefore, Lunars can do something unique with martial arts. Not a hard concept. Also, &quot;leads you to believe that you need mechanical diversity to be cool and unique?&quot; is just putting words in my mouth. I would be disappointed if Lunars didn't get something to differentiate themselves from Solars, <i>because they are locked out of the highest level of sorcery.</i> So automatically Lunars are inferior in this regard to Solars, and so I started a discussion about what advantages they might get.<br /> <br /> @ everyone else, it's probably a moot point right now because we don't have any hard data about the Lunars. But we can still brainstorm, so what would you like to see (<i>under the assumption that Lunars do, in fact, get something unique in regards to sorcery</i>). Since they're doing better in 3rd and might have closer ties to the Raksha, perhaps there will be a tie between the moon and the Wyld that gives Lunar Witches an advantage to shaping sorcerous motes in regards to wyld zones, or something of the like.<br /> <br /> Man, I gotta say, I just love Sorcerers. I wish I had people to play with around me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:04:35-07:00","id":1202822,"title":"","content":"By the way, it's been confirmed Lunars have access to Necromancy this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:11:06-07:00","id":1202826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202822#post1202822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, it's been confirmed Lunars have access to Necromancy this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that in question? They had access to Shadowlands Circle since forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:14:10-07:00","id":1202827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202822#post1202822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, it's been confirmed Lunars have access to Necromancy this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there we go. Question solved. Now to design a Lunar forest witch Red Mage type character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:28:57-07:00","id":1202832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202813#post1202813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Discover what spells he's got, hunt down the gods of the spells and eat them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Or bully them into taking a sabbatical, which might be easier after you eat the first one.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And to be specific, this would be a story possibility because it's specifically something Lunars would/could/should (at least up to 2E) do. Other splats would have to splat at the problem differsplatingly. A Sidereal might arrange for the spell's god to be audited or to be awarded a sabbatical for excellent service.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bOkay, I thought you were talking about something for the sake of shapeshifting into those gods, but this gives me the impression that you think that removing or affecting the god of a spell would... have some effect on it? Make the spell inoperable?</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThat's not how gods work.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202819#post1202819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's canon that it combines with martial arts (as shown in the picture).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere may be a developer statement about hybrid forms and martial arts, but art pieces don't really ever prove anything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T19:47:51-07:00","id":1202849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202819#post1202819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War forms give lunars bonuses to their stats, and it's canon that it combines with martial arts (as shown in the picture).</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course becoming stronger is compatible with martial arts. I don't see how that's exclusive to Lunars. Are you gonna try and tell me that a Solar with Increasing Strength Exercise is gonna have that shut off when he goes into Tiger Form? Of course not.<br /> <br /> And again, none of this is indicated by a picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202819#post1202819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, &quot;leads you to believe that you need mechanical diversity to be cool and unique?&quot; is just putting words in my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>How am I supposed to take it, then, when you keep asking for ways to be unique by being more powerful?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202819#post1202819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be disappointed if Lunars didn't get something to differentiate themselves from Solars, <i>because they are locked out of the highest level of sorcery.</i> So automatically Lunars are inferior in this regard to Solars, and so I started a discussion about what advantages they might get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a particular reason Lunars need to be given a balancing factor to make up for having less raw power than Solars. You don't play an Exalt type for the power, you play it to match the concept in your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-03-2018, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T02:38:45-07:00","id":1202921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Great Cthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202826#post1202826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that in question? They had access to Shadowlands Circle since forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering it was asked not only in this thread but also the Ask the Devs one I would say yes, it was in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:43:19-07:00","id":1203120,"title":"","content":"The following is one part my impression of what the 3e devs/writers/editors (former and current) have been saying, nine parts my opinion on how they should execute things:<br /> <br /> Human greatness (and the pitfalls thereof) is the Solar theme. If the core of your character's identity is a profession or a D&amp;D character class or the like, your character concept is a Solar, and trying to do it with a Lunar/Sidereal/ won't work as well. At the moment in Creation the Solars are only newly-returned, so they aren't currently sitting at the top of the heap, but rest assured that unless they get put back in the bottle, <i>they will</i>. If you're playing a non-Solar whose current identity is &quot;the best sorcerer&quot;, part of the (canon) story of Exalted is that you've been served notice that your days on top are numbered. If you're playing a non-Solar whose ambition is to be &quot;the best sorcerer&quot;, part of your (canon) character's concept is that character will not realize that ambition.<br /> <br /> Other types of Exalted (in context of the line) have identities that are something other than their profession or &quot;character class&quot;. So, &quot;Lunar sorcerer&quot;, per se, isn't a valid character concept (in the line as a whole). The reason you play a Lunar sorcerer is that you've got a Lunar character concept that is supported by being an initiated sorcerer (or becaue you're playing a Lunars game, of course; again &quot;in the line as a whole&quot;). Lunars might have some unique bits to how they interact with sorcery, but that wouldn't be there to make them better at sorcery, but to make their sorcery better at supporting a Lunar character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","user":"Verzio","date":". 04-04-2018, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T21:11:42-07:00","id":1203284,"title":"","content":"Yo, I got your unique Lunar twist on sorcery right here: it's called <i>being a goddamn tyrant lizard</i> while you do it. Or, you know, a bird (JUSTICE RAINS FROM ABOVE).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T21:14:35-07:00","id":1203285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203284#post1203284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (JUSTICE RAINS FROM ABOVE).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohgodiknowwheresthatfrom. <br /> <br /> Overwatch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T23:03:25-07:00","id":1203305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202708#post1202708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh God, was there ever an idea that individual spells had their own spirits?<br /> <br /> \u200bJesus that shit got out of hand. I mean, even if there wasn't, I know there were gods of each level of martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Belated, and as was said, there's the question of ST's choice, but IIRC, it was actually expressly called out in text that this wasn't supposed to be a thing, and that there were no gods attached to Sorcery. Gods could learn Sorcery, but there was no god <i>of</i> sorcery, or of particular spells or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T23:11:27-07:00","id":1203307,"title":"","content":"I personally would expect that, at most, the Lunar book might contain some new initiations and associated merits; not restricted to Lunars, but designed to dovetail with their themes (liminality, transformation, etc). Maybe one or two Charms that boost sorcery by way of Occult. <br /> <br /> They also have second-circle necromancy this edition, apparently, so there's that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T23:40:15-07:00","id":1203309,"title":"","content":"Whoa, they can learn second circle necromancy in third edition? That definitely speaks volumes. And is an interesting lore point that was hinted about in Second Edition but was ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T04:56:53-07:00","id":1203371,"title":"","content":"'cause I cannot eat a dragon to become one anymore, apparently.<br /> So, magic ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:23:34-07:00","id":1203387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203305#post1203305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Belated, and as was said, there's the question of ST's choice, but IIRC, it was actually expressly called out in text that this wasn't supposed to be a thing, and that there were no gods attached to Sorcery. Gods could learn Sorcery, but there was no god <i>of</i> sorcery, or of particular spells or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOhh that's right.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough in retrospect, I think that was overthinking it a little as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T11:34:14-07:00","id":1203469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer#post1202375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that has been on my mind recently. 3rd edition is moving away from Lunars as &quot;basically werewolves&quot; into a bigger group of, well, Primal Heroes I guess. Shape Changers, Forest Witches, etc. But since only Solars can access the highest tier of Sorcery, what benefits do Lunars get that differentiate them?<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm NOT asking &quot;why would you make a Lunar Sorcerer&quot;, because people have all kinds of reasons to play characters they like, rather, my question is &quot;What advantages do Lunars get when learning Sorcery&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you be a Lunar anything?<br /> <br /> If your character concept is &quot;sorcerer&quot; and nothing else, and all you care about is having as many advantages as possible as a Sorcerer, you <i>should</i> play a Solar, not so much because they have more raw power (honestly when it comes to Sorcery they're nearly equal until E5 due to having few Sorcery-boosting Occult charms and Supernal not applying to Sorcery initiations) but because their vanilla nature means that Solars are the easiest way to play a &quot;pure Sorcerer&quot; who is thematically just all-Sorcerer all-the-time with little else to them. There's plenty of non-Sorcery charms a Solar could want, but they tend to be thematically light in ways that avoid distracting from the fact that you're a Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> However, the thematic stuff that being a Lunar brings to the table also offers Lunars specific Lunar ways of doing things in any sort of role. A shapeshifting Sorcerer can do things a normal Sorcerer can't, either by casting spells that will enhance them after they change form, or by using the mobility granted by their shapeshifting to reach better areas to cast from. (We don't know what Lunar charms might do, but they could have similar synergies.)<br /> <br /> But again, I feel that it's a bit weird to ask this about Sorcery specifically, because for the most part the Solar advantage with Sorcery is <i>less</i> than it is with any other area of expertise focused on an Ability - the Lunar Sorcerer only has to seriously worry about &quot;why not be a Solar?&quot; at E5, whereas the Lunar Swordsman is going to face the fact that the Solar has better swording-people charms as early as E1. For most of the game the <i>real</i> difference isn't SCS access, it's how their other, non-sorcery capabilities provide support for their role as a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Beyond that you just have to decide whether having eventual SCS access is central to your narrative as a sorcerer (keeping in mind, again, that unless you start at high essence, you probably won't have it for most of the game anyway, and may never actually reach it depending on how long your game lasts.) SCS and its thematic of &quot;drastically change the world in a single action&quot; is one of the few narratives genuinely, completely unique to the Solar Exalted (and perhaps their Infernal kin), so if it's central to the story you want to tell then yes, you have to be a Solar, just like if you wanted to tell the narrative of a Sidereal or Lunar you'd have to stick to those splats. To me that means that the question of &quot;why not be a Solar?&quot; comes down to a question of whether you care about having this be part of your long-term narrative or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T11:44:57-07:00","id":1203474,"title":"","content":"Also, aside, if I were redesigning Sorcery I would probably change a number of things that would help with this. Specifically:<br /> <br /> 1. Instead of each tier of Sorcery being limited to a specific Essence level, they <i>start</i> at E1, E2, and E3 respectively; but individual spells can then have higher Essence. This allows SCS to come up in an actual game more often, but it also allows the Lunar to keep learning more powerful spells past E3 (since you can now make E4 and E5 Celestial spells.) The bulk of SCS would still be at E5. Granted, coming up with high-essence Celestial or Terrestrial spells could be extremely difficult; generally they wouldn't increase in power on their own quite the way that charms do. Instead, high essence on non-Solar Circle Sorcery would be used for...<br /> <br /> 2. Allow Sorcery to, like Evocations, have prerequisite charms (as well as spells.) This allows the creation of spells that can only be used by a specific splat (as well as spells that can only be used if you've mastered a specific martial art, or even spells that require specific evocations of a specific artifact.) This would be what high-essence Celestial and Terrestrial spells would be for - you don't get an inherent power boost for an E5 Terrestrial Spell like you do with a charm, but you could use an E5 DB charm as a prerequisite, which would let you bend the limitations of Terrestrial-tier Sorcery slightly by piggybacking on whatever that charm does.<br /> <br /> Then the answer of what unique thematic / mechanical ground a Lunar Sorcerer gets becomes easy, since they can make unique Lunar spells branching off of Lunar charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T16:02:25-07:00","id":1203549,"title":"","content":"As I said, if I want to have powerful sorcery stuff to buy as an Essence 5 Lunar sorcerer, I would instead look into Essence 5 Intelligence Charms that branch off of Celestial Circle Initiation.<br /> <br /> Charms to assist the use of spells that affect physical transformations, that affect minds, that facilitate travel, that perform deception, that enable stealth...<br /> <br /> Maybe spell-specific upgrades.<br /> <br /> Though I could always just spend the same time and XP on sorcerous workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:54:35-07:00","id":1203594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203120#post1203120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The following is one part my impression of what the 3e devs/writers/editors (former and current) have been saying, nine parts my opinion on how they should execute things:<br /> <br /> Human greatness (and the pitfalls thereof) is the Solar theme. If the core of your character's identity is a profession or a D&amp;D character class or the like, your character concept is a Solar, and trying to do it with a Lunar/Sidereal/ won't work as well. At the moment in Creation the Solars are only newly-returned, so they aren't currently sitting at the top of the heap, but rest assured that unless they get put back in the bottle, <i>they will</i>. If you're playing a non-Solar whose current identity is &quot;the best sorcerer&quot;, part of the (canon) story of Exalted is that you've been served notice that your days on top are numbered. If you're playing a non-Solar whose ambition is to be &quot;the best sorcerer&quot;, part of your (canon) character's concept is that character will not realize that ambition.<br /> <br /> Other types of Exalted (in context of the line) have identities that are something other than their profession or &quot;character class&quot;. So, &quot;Lunar sorcerer&quot;, per se, isn't a valid character concept (in the line as a whole). The reason you play a Lunar sorcerer is that you've got a Lunar character concept that is supported by being an initiated sorcerer (or becaue you're playing a Lunars game, of course; again &quot;in the line as a whole&quot;). Lunars might have some unique bits to how they interact with sorcery, but that wouldn't be there to make them better at sorcery, but to make their sorcery better at supporting a Lunar character concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, though, that both Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded <i>do</i> have unique features that aren't really reproducible under the auspices of &quot;Human Greatness&quot;, and for a Solar to even attempt them would require a maximum-Ambition, Solar-Circle Working and a <i>very </i>permissive ST. Sidereals can manipulate the underlying rules of existence, allowing them to work at a remove that even the mightiest sorcerer would be hard-pressed to imitate. A lot of their charms in previous editions let them declare an outcome by fiat, and while a Solar could accomplish the same thing through hard work and perseverance, they'd have to be physically-present and doing <i>hard work</i>, exposing them to risk and requiring them to invest a lot of time and effort that the Siderereal can spend doing other things. A Solar can learn Sidereal Martial Arts, but they cannot <i>teach </i>them, meaning that if a Solar wants access they have to actually come before a Sid as an inferior. On a narrative level, only Sidereals can maintain the Loom of Fate, without which we've been assured everything would go to shit. Sidereals have a niche.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are individually-weaker than Solars, and still can't access the highest circle of Sorcery, but they absolutely can cheat their way up a tier in both Sorcery and MA (yes, both Mnemon and the Empress used powerful artifacts to accomplish this, but the fact they managed it at all is a powerful precedent). In prior editions, the Immaculate styles were <i>really fucking powerful</i>, to the point of being straight upgrades over their native charms and frankly over a lot of other Celestial styles. Neither of these put them on a level with Solars, but that didn't matter because they had something else that very much did - their ability to <i>make more Dragon-Blooded</i>. NONE of the other Exalted types can manage something like this, and it has huge ramifications for the rest of the setting, starting with the fact that all the Dragon-Blooded working together managed to <i>kill the Solars and conquer the world</i>. A Dragon-Blooded Sorcerer who graduates from the Heptagram may be overworked and underappreciated by the rest of Dynastic society, but they have access to resources that the returned Solars can only dream of. If a Dragon-Blooded Sorcerer wants to put together a really ambitious project, they have a vast social network to call on, including lots of other sorcerers - hello, extra Means! A Twilight is lucky to run across <i>one </i>other Sorcerer who isn't actively trying to kill them.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, No-Moons also absolutely had something that Solars couldn't replicate (until Glories came out, but eh, the supplement treadmill is a harsh mistress). They could cast spells more-cheaply, which enabled them to spam battle-magic like nobody else. They couldn't cast the strongest spells, no, but they had something unique. And honestly, that's at the heart of this issue, which is really less about Lunar <i>Sorcerers </i>than Lunars in general. Their signature ability, shapechanging, is ultimately limited to facilitating things that they do personally, and so they are always going to fall short of the Solars in just about every respect. They're alone in lacking anything that sets them apart from Solars beyond aesthetics. Maybe 3E will change that! I really hope so! But as the situation stands, I've seen more cases where Solar PCs decide to side with the Dragon-Blooded against the Lunars than the other way around, which suggests to me that something has gone seriously wrong with the execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:33:35-07:00","id":1203634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203594#post1203594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Second Edition, No-Moons also absolutely had something that Solars couldn't replicate (until Glories came out, but eh, the supplement treadmill is a harsh mistress). They could cast spells more-cheaply, which enabled them to spam battle-magic like nobody else. They couldn't cast the strongest spells, no, but they had something unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, here's why that was a terrible idea and why Glories was absolutely 100% correct to give it to Solars (although it's a path that shouldn't have been started down in the first place and was really only begun because 2e Sorcery had so many problems that you could pretty much give people whatever you want.)<br /> <br /> 1. Solars only get SCS access at E5. If you go that route, Twilights - supposed to be the greatest Sorcerers in Creation - are worse at Sorcery until E5.<br /> <br /> 2. In practice, &quot;meta-magic&quot; charms are difficult to balance around. They're something that has to be balanced into the spell system from the start.<br /> <br /> 3. The charms did absolutely nothing uniquely Lunar about it. They were just &quot;generically better at Sorcery.&quot; This would be <i>perhaps</i> appropriate for a Solar charm, but unless your premise is &quot;Lunars are better at all Sorcery except the Solar tier&quot; or &quot;Lunars are better at combat sorcery&quot;, it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> 4. &quot;Lunars are flatly better at combat sorcery&quot; is not an acceptable statement. Combat makes up a huge portion of the game and, yes, massive swaths of Sorcery itself. Beyond that, the usual problems with &quot;better at Solars at [narrow thing within the Solar purview&quot; applies here - once you start peeling off aspects of Solar excellence like that and doling them out to other splats, Solars very, very rapidly become the &quot;jack-of-all-trades, master-of-none&quot; Exalted. (Why shouldn't Sidereals then say &quot;all right, we claim preeminence at subtle, manipulative Sorcery&quot;, and DBs say &quot;ok, we'll be the best at Elemental Sorcery&quot;, etc?) There are clearly-defined limits to the Solar theme; if you want to do stuff Solars don't, you can go there. If <i>I want to be the very best, like no one ever was</i> is absolutely, completely central to your character concept, play a Solar. That's part of what they're there for.<br /> <br /> The primary advantage a No-Moon has over a Solar, in terms of unique stuff to explore, is that they've got an innate capability for shapeshifting. Their charmset might find some other interesting directions to go in or synergies with their other stuff (and one problem that Lunars have - the reason we keep coming to this argument with Lunars and not with other splats - is that they really don't have much outside of shapeshifting), but they absolutely shouldn't get their own special &quot;generic&quot; Sorcery boosts.<br /> <br /> (Of course, an additional thing to consider is that in 3e, Sorcery-boosting is generally occupied by initiations and sorcerous evocations. I would expect Lunars to have initiations they tend to use and teach each other - but those could also be learned by a Solar if someone was willing to teach them, because that's how Sorcery works. And they're not generally going to be uniquely superior to the initiations found elsewhere, although they might be better at eg. working well with shapeshifting or exploiting other unique aspects of the Lunar existence.)<br /> <br /> Giving Lunars <i>uniquely Lunar</i> stuff that interacts with Sorcery is fine; making them <i>best at a broad swath of Sorcery</i> is not. And the corebook very pointedly didn't have any charms to directly enhance Sorcery, so I'll be pissed if we start seeing them in other splats (and would expect it to be an oversight that would be rectified by adding Solar sorcery-enhancing charms in a later book. Because, again, SCS only shows up at E5, and doesn't even appear in most games, so if everyone else starts getting broad sorcery-boosting charms and Solars don't, the result is, most of the time, in most games, that Twilights will be comparatively bad at Sorcery.)<br /> <br /> An E1 Twilight needs to be able to express the thematic of &quot;master of Sorcery&quot; every bit as thoroughly and uniquely as an E1 Dawn expresses the thematic of &quot;master of swordsmanship.&quot; Right now they're already struggling to do that. Giving everyone else Sorcery-boosting charms would turn the situation into a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-05-2018, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:59:11-07:00","id":1203649,"title":"","content":"Jesus fuck, dude. That was three lines out of a three-paragraph post, purely meant to illustrate how Lunar sorcerers at least got <i>something </i>to distinguish them in prior editions. Going into detail about how it's hot garbage is unnecessary because it's 2E so the fact that it's hot garbage is already implicit. I'm not asking for the No-Moon anima power to come back, I'm asking what capabilities we can give to the Lunars (and ONLY the Lunars) without the ST and the entire Exalted fandom jumping in to explain for the umpteenth time that Lunars don't get to have nice things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:28:13-07:00","id":1203667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203649#post1203649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... without the ST and the entire Exalted fandom jumping in to explain for the umpteenth time that Lunars don't get to have nice things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I started this thread. I saw that Lunars didn't get access to top level Sorcery and thought to myself &quot;well, if I wanted to be a Lunar Sorcerer that sucks&quot;. In the Dev thread they mentioned that Lunars get to combo their stat boosting native charms with Martial Arts, but for Sorcery? Too bad, gtfo.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:32:39-07:00","id":1203671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203667#post1203667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I started this thread. I saw that Lunars didn't get access to top level Sorcery and thought to myself &quot;well, if I wanted to be a Lunar Sorcerer that sucks&quot;. In the Dev thread they mentioned that Lunars get to combo their stat boosting native charms with Martial Arts, but for Sorcery? Too bad, gtfo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did they say they couldn't use INT charms to enhance Sorcery? I'd imagine they'd at minimum get excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:17:27-07:00","id":1203716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203649#post1203649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus fuck, dude. That was three lines out of a three-paragraph post, purely meant to illustrate how Lunar sorcerers at least got <i>something </i>to distinguish them in prior editions. Going into detail about how it's hot garbage is unnecessary because it's 2E so the fact that it's hot garbage is already implicit. I'm not asking for the No-Moon anima power to come back, I'm asking what capabilities we can give to the Lunars (and ONLY the Lunars) without the ST and the entire Exalted fandom jumping in to explain for the umpteenth time that Lunars don't get to have nice things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but my point is, when it comes to Sorcery in particular, it's very hard to give Lunars anything at all that makes them better at it in some unique way, when Solars have... basically nothing that makes them better at spellcasting in any way, outside of SCS access (which, while awesome, is only available at E5), occasional free Occult excellencies, and some indirect benefit from spirit interaction stuff. I think that that sucks for the reasons I outlined above and was a general mistake that makes it hard to feel like you're playing a dedicated Sorcerer, but I'll also be mildly pissed if it's corrected by adding Sorcery-boosting charms to other splats (even well-thought out, carefully-made ones that benefit Lunars in specifically Lunar ways) without eventually going back and giving Solar Sorcerers something they can use to feel like they're focused on Sorcery outside of having a bunch of spells.<br /> <br /> That's also why I'd prefer that such Sorcery stuff be only &quot;soft&quot;-bound to Lunars (eg. via initiations that can theoretically be taught to outsiders, or moonsilver sorcerer-focused artifacts that could also be used by others). Because given the near-absence of charms that enhance spellcasting in the core, the gap between &quot;giving Lunars some stuff that makes their Sorcery unique in an interesting way&quot; and &quot;Lunars are now mostly better spellcasters than Solars up until E5&quot; is <i>vanishingly</i> slim. (Unless you make the charms E5, but then... what's the point? Like SCS, they'd be mostly unavailable.) The charms would have to be really weak or really specific, and it's pretty hard to make spellcasting-booster charms in a balanced fashion in the first place (probably why the core lacks them, of course.)<br /> <br /> This could be avoided if Solars had a handful of charms to boost spellcasting in their own way, which would then create wriggle room to give other splats things that range up to that point or which provide their own thematic take in different directions. But that's not where we are right now. And yeah, I know what you meant, but the reason I had to point it out is because we <i>are</i> still pretty close to where we were in 2e in that respect (ie. a potential failing of the Solar charmset that might get fixed in other places without getting fixed for Solars.)<br /> <br /> This isn't a problem with, like, Lunar Melee, because Solars have completely awesome unique Melee charms, which lets you give Lunars ridiculously powerful combat charms of their own (including ones applicable to Melee) without much risk of disturbing the Solar narrative; or even with Martial Arts, since that has much more synergy with things like Solar Athletics or Solar Resistance.<br /> <br /> I mean I mostly agree with your analysis of what the Lunar problem is. But with Sorcery <i>in particular</i>, it's compounded by the fact that at least as presented in the core, 3e Sorcery leaves very little wriggle room for unique splat-specific advantages to spellcasting unless we want to conclude that Solars are uniquely bad at the act of casting spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T23:55:41-07:00","id":1203738,"title":"","content":"So, does death from above need reemphasizing, or...? Seriously, raining spells on things from long altitude (or extreme with Brilliant Raptor as control) is a ridiculously solid tactic that Lunars can do cheaper and more reliably than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Hey, you know what else is fun about being a small animal? Trivially sneaking into <i>all</i> the best places to drop a Cantana of Empty Voices on.<br /> <br /> At the other end of the scale, eat anything with Legendary Size and you'll never be a glass cannon again, plus who <i>doesn't</i> love sorcerer-dinosaurs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T03:41:50-07:00","id":1203779,"title":"","content":"*hums* You know... it'd be an interesting setting hack to say that all three circles of Sorcery are open for everyone. Has that been considered before? Yeah, it makes Sorcerers at high essence really powerful, but Sorcery is a very specific form of power, only really wielded by Elders. *hums*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T04:02:41-07:00","id":1203783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203649#post1203649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the entire Exalted fandom jumping in to explain for the umpteenth time that Lunars don't get to have nice things.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203667#post1203667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I started this thread. I saw that Lunars didn't get access to top level Sorcery and thought to myself &quot;well, if I wanted to be a Lunar Sorcerer that sucks&quot;. In the Dev thread they mentioned that Lunars get to combo their stat boosting native charms with Martial Arts, but for Sorcery? Too bad, gtfo.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI can't help but feel sorry for the upcoming Lunars book when it's going to be facing an uphill battle against this kind of defensive attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T04:38:09-07:00","id":1203788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203779#post1203779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*hums* You know... it'd be an interesting setting hack to say that all three circles of Sorcery are open for everyone. Has that been considered before? Yeah, it makes Sorcerers at high essence really powerful, but Sorcery is a very specific form of power, only really wielded by Elders. *hums*</div> </div> </div> </div>I once thought of a setting like that. In the wake of the great contagion, an accident activated Salina's last and greatest working, granting everyone the power of sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T05:55:15-07:00","id":1203799,"title":"","content":"*Looks at the grenade in his hand*<br /> <br /> *Laughs maniacally as he pulls the pin*<br /> <br /> <i><b>Why be a Dragon-Blooded sorcerer?</b></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","user":"Equitable Remedy","date":". 04-16-2018, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T06:47:31-07:00","id":1203808,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...what about getting means for using your totem in workings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T06:48:59-07:00","id":1203810,"title":"","content":"Why be a Lunar sorceror? Start with Wood Dragons Claw and Skin of Bronze. Now design variations like &quot;skin of metal&quot; &quot;claws and fangs of flame&quot;. Then use that join five together as one spell, transform humanoid. You are <b>VOLTRON</b>. Hmm. Also, Lunar does something fiddly and becomes a magma kraken<br /> <br /> More in general, how often do even Solars want to use 3rd circle? We're talking large area, don't care about collateral damage, massive overkill type spells. Would a Steward want to regularly do that to their territory?<br /> <br /> Course, the most obvious ways to give Lunars <u>different</u> specialties in sorcery, would be to use that new mechanic known as &quot;shaping rituals&quot;. Say, devour creature's heartsblood to gain sorcerous motes. Or eat a Fair Folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:03:03-07:00","id":1203816,"title":"","content":"Uh oh. <br /> <br /> Um.... don't the moonsilver tattoos stop this sort of self-transformation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:18:24-07:00","id":1203819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203816#post1203816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh oh.<br /> <br /> Um.... don't the moonsilver tattoos stop this sort of self-transformation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While still up in the air (as with most things Lunar) we do have this bit from Vance<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1149688#post1149688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We haven't fully pinned down how the tattoos work in Ex3, but I don't think it makes sense for them to block healing and other beneficial effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:55:23-07:00","id":1203831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203819#post1203819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While still up in the air (as with most things Lunar) we do have this bit from Vance<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Guess they fixed that. <br /> <br /> Why did they even have it block beneficial effects in the first place, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:21:24-07:00","id":1203843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203831#post1203831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did they even have it block beneficial effects in the first place, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bProbably a misplaced sense of consistency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:26:24-07:00","id":1203845,"title":"","content":"I think kind of by accident. It blocked any effect that changed your form, except with Lunar charms/knacks.<br /> I'm not sure if it was deliberate that you couldn't use Invulnerable Skin of Bronze and Wood Dragon Claw, or if they just forgot to mention your own spells on top of Lunar charms/knacks.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they just thought it made more sense that an artefact that completely protected your form stopped you even casting spells that changed your form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:27:31-07:00","id":1203846,"title":"","content":"Or was it just your own Lunar charms/knacks? Maybe that. I remember I tried mutating the party's Changing Moon and her tattoos protected her from my Intelligence charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:57:14-07:00","id":1203854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203799#post1203799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Looks at the grenade in his hand*<br /> <br /> *Laughs maniacally as he pulls the pin*<br /> <br /> <i><b>Why by a Dragon-Blooded sorcerer?</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>They get the benefits of the Realm's obscene wealth and a vast social support network for learning new spells and pulling together Workings, as well as the chance (however remote) that they can do what the Empress or Mnemon did and get access to the Celestial Circle. Seriously, I literally just covered that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:15:45-07:00","id":1203859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203854#post1203854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They get the benefits of the Realm's obscene wealth and a vast social support network for learning new spells and pulling together Workings, as well as the chance (however remote) that they can do what the Empress or Mnemon did and get access to the Celestial Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>At which point they might hope to some day be the equal of a serious Lunar sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:18:56-07:00","id":1203860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203859#post1203859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At which point they might hope to some day be the equal of a serious Lunar sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quantity has a quality all of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:32:56-07:00","id":1203865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203716#post1203716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I mostly agree with your analysis of what the Lunar problem is. But with Sorcery <i>in particular</i>, it's compounded by the fact that at least as presented in the core, 3e Sorcery leaves very little wriggle room for unique splat-specific advantages to spellcasting unless we want to conclude that Solars are uniquely bad at the act of casting spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all seriousness, I'd like to see Solars get more tricks for interacting with Sorcery than just access to higher tiers, leaving more room for other splats to have unique, Sorcery-adjacent powers while still allowing for Twilights to call themselves &quot;The Best Sorcerers&quot; and be able to back that claim up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T10:33:28-07:00","id":1203886,"title":"","content":"I know Aquillion isn\u2019t responding to me, but I\u2019ll still say how odd it is that he condemns the idea of non-Solars getting any Sorcery boosting Charms on the grounds that it screws over Solars below Essence 5.<br /> <br /> This complaint totally ignores the idea I put forward that any such booster Lunar Charms would be Essence 5 only. And that the benefits would not equal the power of Solar Circle Spells and lack of penalty for Solar Circle Workings.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Dragon-Blooded might get boosts at Essence 5 and 3, because anything they get wouldn\u2019t be as powerful as the Celestial Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:55:25-07:00","id":1203923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1202819#post1202819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we can still brainstorm, so what would you like to see (<i>under the assumption that Lunars do, in fact, get something unique in regards to sorcery</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've written four Lunar-themed Sorcerous Initiations, <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/12548572/chapters/29644620\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/13926246/chapters/32053521\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/13926246/chapters/32153325\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, and<a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/13996455/chapters/32380362\" target=\"_blank\"> here</a>. All part of the Lunar Castebooks project.<br /> <br /> Only the one tied to the No Moon Anima is unique to Lunars, though. The rest are Sorcerous Initiations anyone could perform, just that Lunars might be more likely to.<br /> <br /> To answer the overall question of why be a Lunar sorcerer, I like to think that the moonsilver tattoos themselves are sorcerous workings, necessitating a deep sorcerous tradition among Second Age Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":". 04-06-2018, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:58:43-07:00","id":1203929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203307#post1203307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would expect that, at most, the Lunar book might contain some new initiations and associated merits; not restricted to Lunars, but designed to dovetail with their themes (liminality, transformation, etc). Maybe one or two Charms that boost sorcery by way of Occult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I put all my sorcery boosting effects in the Lunar Castebooks in the No Moon Caste effects (and some in the First Age Caste effects). Though I think Charms beyond the Intelligence Excellency would certainly be possible, I have not written any.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:59:46-07:00","id":1203930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203779#post1203779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*hums* You know... it'd be an interesting setting hack to say that all three circles of Sorcery are open for everyone. Has that been considered before? Yeah, it makes Sorcerers at high essence really powerful, but Sorcery is a very specific form of power, only really wielded by Elders. *hums*</div> </div> </div> </div>It is implied in Dreams of the First Age, Lords of Creation, Salina's entry, that, given enough Solar madness (in 3e speak, a high Ambition working), everyone could have access to Solar Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T12:54:57-07:00","id":1203954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203860#post1203860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantity has a quality all of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what that has to do with a debate on why you'd want to play a [splat] sorcerer, unless your ST gives people the option of playing either a Solar or three hundred Dragon-Bloods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:17:02-07:00","id":1203968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203954#post1203954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see what that has to do with a debate on why you'd want to play a [splat] sorcerer, unless your ST gives people the option of playing either a Solar or three hundred Dragon-Bloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big fan of Werewolf: the Forsaken, a game in which the players create not only their PCs, but also the extended membership of their pack (including wolf-blooded and vanilla humans) and the ability to call on this network for support is a <i>massive </i>advantage. On top of that, werewolves have their Tribes and their Lodges for pooling information, sharing resources, and taking on threats too big for one pack to handle on its own. I'm hoping Dynasts in 3E will have similar mechanical support for calling on their staff, House, and former classmates for aid, because otherwise those institutions start feeling less like mixed blessings and more like millstones around a PC's neck. At the very least, it's established that Sorcerous Workings benefit IMMENSELY from having other sorcerers and/or exotic resources on hand, and I can definitely see DBs getting special Shaping Rituals for going all BY OUR POWERS COMBINED like they can with Elemental Bolt etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:15:04-07:00","id":1204006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203886#post1203886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Aquillion isn\u2019t responding to me, but I\u2019ll still say how odd it is that he condemns the idea of non-Solars getting any Sorcery boosting Charms on the grounds that it screws over Solars below Essence 5.<br /> <br /> This complaint totally ignores the idea I put forward that any such booster Lunar Charms would be Essence 5 only. And that the benefits would not equal the power of Solar Circle Spells and lack of penalty for Solar Circle Workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not often that I wholly agree with you, but this is it.<br /> <br /> Besides which, will comment this is kind of really to intimately linked with how 3e ties experience to Essence in order to structure character progression a bit more (by popular acclaim for the most part a good idea!). If in 2e Solars were weaker sorcerers than Lunars until they bought Essence 5, and anyone can choose to buy Essence 5 whenever they want if they're prepared to use their points and experience that way, that's a lot like saying &quot;Solar players can choose to build Twilights who are weaker at sorcery than some Lunars&quot; which... yes? they can? (Whatever else the merits or lack thereof of 2e No Moon power notwithstanding.). This is only a problem if you mash up the way each edition uses the Essence score in the worst possible way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T16:03:26-07:00","id":1204022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203968#post1203968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, it's established that Sorcerous Workings benefit IMMENSELY from having other sorcerers and/or exotic resources on hand</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;benefit immensely&quot; you mean &quot;gain +2 Means,&quot; then yes. On a Terrestrial Circle Working you won't need that in the first place, and on a Celestial or Solar Circle Working it almost exactly compensates for your increased difficulty and lower dice cap compared to a Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:19:20-07:00","id":1204291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203845#post1203845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think kind of by accident. It blocked any effect that changed your form, except with Lunar charms/knacks.<br /> I'm not sure if it was deliberate that you couldn't use Invulnerable Skin of Bronze and Wood Dragon Claw, or if they just forgot to mention your own spells on top of Lunar charms/knacks.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they just thought it made more sense that an artefact that completely protected your form stopped you even casting spells that changed your form.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that last one. Per Manual: Lunars, pg 129-130:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manual of Exalted Power: Lunars</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The moonsilver tattoos that most Lunars wear protect<br /> them from the effect of the Wyld taint\u2026 and from so much<br /> more. The tattoos protect Lunars from any in\ufb02uence that<br /> would change their shape other than their inherent abili-<br /> ties. Tattooed Lunar Exalted are completely immune to all<br /> such effects: A Lunar is as unaffected by a spirit\u2019s attack<br /> that changes her bones to roots as she is by her own casting<br /> of Invulnerable Skin of Bronze. The tattoos themselves are<br /> equally proof against all attempts to affect them with magic,<br /> and all attempts to pry the moonsilver ink from Lunars\u2019 skins<br /> meet with failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except that Dreams of the First Age included a Lunar Appearance Charm that had the Shaping keyword and explicitly <i>was </i>blocked by tattoos, so, you know. Second Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:37:28-07:00","id":1204295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1203594#post1203594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, though, that both Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded <i>do</i> have unique features that aren't really reproducible under the auspices of &quot;Human Greatness&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which aren't things that make them personally-mechanically better at sorcery than Solars. Insofar as their unique things give them an advantage over Solars in sorcery, it's less direct than the old No-Moon trick.<br /> <br /> In 2e, Lunars weren't particularly more than second-best Solars, and this was a bad thing that needs to be fixed. I do not think that giving Lunars a personal-mechanical advantage over Solars in sorcery is the right way to do that. Indeed, I think it would <i>worsen</i> the issue. Anything that encourages playing Solar character concepts as Lunars will simply draw attention to Lunars not being as good at being Solars as Solars are.<br /> <br /> Let's take some perspective. Dragon-Blooded are human society's legitimate establishment, the holders of its wealth and power who enjoy its benefits. As characters they are defined very much by their social place and relationships (as the DB draft makes clear).<br /> <br /> Solars are the Great Men, the people who, regardless of background, are so exceptional that they force human society to change around them, often to the discomfit of its establishment. As characters they are defined by their genius (with mechanical expression in things like their Supernal).<br /> <br /> Sidereals are the Secret Masters, the conspirators outside of ordinary society who nevertheless control it because they know the right secrets. Mechanical things like being the only ones who can teach Sidereal Martial Arts are right in line with that. The classic mountain-dwelling sifu with secret knowledge, who rather than transforming society through his own demonstrated prowess simply passes it on to the right student who then does the transforming -- or in a more Western context, Yoda training Luke -- that's just obviously a Sidereal training a Solar, when you put it in these terms.<br /> <br /> (The retired hero who is recruited to actually come out and make one last heroic effort at fixing things? He's a Solar who tried to live like a Sidereal. Which is why he had to come out of retirement rather than teaching a student; he's a Great Man, not a Secret Master.)<br /> <br /> The question is then, what is the (3e) Lunar's relation to society, and thus what defines them as characters? Then you support <i>that</i> with mechanics. You can't just throw them some mechanical bennies and say, &quot;Go forth and be a Great Man,&quot; because they'll be second-best to the Solars at that. That's setting Lunars up to fail. Lunars need nice things that make them better at being what (3e) Lunars are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:22:42-07:00","id":1204367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1204291#post1204291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...except that Dreams of the First Age included a Lunar Appearance Charm that had the Shaping keyword and explicitly <i>was </i>blocked by tattoos, so, you know. Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tattoos weren't invented until the Second Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T20:48:56-07:00","id":1204411,"title":"","content":"I'm so much happier about the Tattoos now that the writers aren't using them like another leash to hold the Lunar Exalted back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:15:38-07:00","id":1204485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1204295#post1204295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is then, what is the (3e) Lunar's relation to society, and thus what defines them as characters? Then you support <i>that</i> with mechanics. You can't just throw them some mechanical bennies and say, &quot;Go forth and be a Great Man,&quot; because they'll be second-best to the Solars at that. That's setting Lunars up to fail. Lunars need nice things that make them better at being what (3e) Lunars are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Vance, Lunars engage with society in the manner of an Apex Predator lending its assistance to prey animals, living in symbiosis with society. They can guard and protect, test and winnow, show them hidden secrets to assist them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:55:09-07:00","id":1204515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1204411#post1204411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so much happier about the Tattoos now that the writers aren't using them like another leash to hold the Lunar Exalted back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm much happier about the Tattoos now that Vance told me that the individualistic, unique Lunars don't have to all have tattoos that look basically identical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:58:56-07:00","id":1204517,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I played a Lunar sorcerer for years (the one in my avatar), and it was great.<br /> So, sure, I couldn't use Solar sorcery... but neither could any of the Solars. We went from starting XP, to about 500xp, then back down again to 200xp and 160 Solar/Lunar XP when we changed editions, and now I guess we're at about 260xp (and like 200 Solar/Lunar xp) maybe? We've played this game for like 10 years, and no-one has Solar sorcery. So I don't think being a Lunar made me miss out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, I could use awesome magic like turning into a bird, turning into a bear, turning into a tyrant lizard, etc. Solars couldn't do that. Because they're lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:56:40-07:00","id":1204568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Originally posted by <b>Manual of Exalted Power: Lunars</b></i><br /> <i>The moonsilver tattoos that most Lunars wear protect<br /> them from the effect of the Wyld taint\u2026 and from so much<br /> more. The tattoos protect Lunars from any in\ufb02uence that<br /> would change their shape other than their inherent abili-<br /> ties. Tattooed Lunar Exalted are completely immune to all<br /> such effects: A Lunar is as unaffected by a spirit\u2019s attack<br /> that changes her bones to roots as she is by her own casting<br /> of Invulnerable Skin of Bronze. The tattoos themselves are<br /> equally proof against all attempts to affect them with magic,<br /> and all attempts to pry the moonsilver ink from Lunars\u2019 skins<br /> meet with failure.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And that highlights why I thought tattoos were poorly thought out. Tattoos protect against physical shape changes. And do nothing against at least as big a threat, the mental changes (insanity, becoming a stereotype out of a story, etc) So much for the Lunar studying the Wyld, or working on a project in a small pocket of reality out there. Along about the third time you start imagining huge invisible purple spiders are chasing you, it becomes time to get out before you no longer want to leave.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I would hope that Lunar magic will be able to integrate the tattoos, so that even some 1st age Lunars had them. At the low end, tattoos are part of an initiation rite and tell other Lunars what kind of sorcery you know. At the high end, possible effects like &quot;storing&quot; a cast spell in a tattoo, changing your signature spell from a small list tatooed into you, dancing skyclad under Luna generates sorcerous motes, tattoos giving you &quot;street cred&quot; when you summon an elemental, some way to lace moonsilver into all your spells for some benefit (obsidian and moonsilver butterflies can maneuver around obstacles to hit more targets?) In general, I would expect Solars to be better at raw power sorcery and big workings, where Lunars would have more flexibillity and possibly subtlety in their magic. So, metamagic type abilities?<br /> <br /> One of my general purpose Lunar grading standards is &quot;would it help a Lunar who infiltrated a Primordial camp and is masquerading as a 3rd or 2nd circle demon?&quot; Alternately, help a Lunar Kaiju who is transporting a Solar or a squad of Dragonbloods. The example Celestial spells could be useful in those situations, Solar spells, not so much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T02:16:38-07:00","id":1209157,"title":"","content":"I see Lunars taking a much more holistic approach to sorcery than Solars, they might not be as good at it but a No Moon is less likely to identify themselves around a specific role like a doctor or a crafter due to being Attribute based and not having Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T05:35:29-07:00","id":1209198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1202375-why-be-a-lunar-sorcerer?p=1204367#post1204367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tattoos weren't invented until the Second Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the author knew this, intending for Air-Body Style to be unusable to most Second Age Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:30:44-07:00","id":1209286,"title":"","content":"My short answer: God-Forged Champion of War","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T10:26:30-07:00","id":1209311,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m personally looking forward to making sorcerous workings that use my \u201cMan-to-Beastman Prana\u201d Charm as a means, so I can enchant an arch to turn people into beast men when they walk through it, to prepare for battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T11:30:38-07:00","id":1209336,"title":"","content":"So. I actually do have some ideas of what a Lunar could do by mixing Lunar features with Sorcery. I'm going to preface this by saying that, like every non-Solar splat, a lot of these assumptions about what they get out of Sorcery that Solars don't is based on the default starting position of the setting. For instance, the Dragon-Blooded have all sorts of artifacts, the backing of an empire, and huge armies that, Solars <i>could</i> get and do more impressive things with, but the default state of the setting is that a lot of things are usually available for specific splats and only occasionally available for Solars.<br /> <br /> By most accounts, Lunars have a similar situation going on with Martial Arts (not getting mastery) and what they bring to the table is the ability to put extra oomph onto attacks through their shapeshifting and the fact that their charms are tied to attributes. We know that a lunar pairing DBT with, say, White Reaper Style will be terrifying, now imagine that same Lunar but using Invulnerable Skin of Bronze, Wood Dragon Claw, or Incomparable Body Arsenal. Similarly, most attack spells in Sorcery use (Attribute + Occult): if a lunar has dice tricks for their attributes, they have a considerable opportunity to enhance their rolls in ways solars can't. In fact, just the nature of their attribute favoritism means that a lunar is usually more likely to have an optimal excellency for every spell.<br /> <br /> Also, the nature of shapeshifting and the trickery options it provides gives Lunars tons of additional options for deploying their sorcery in ways Solars can't keep up with without heavy investment in other charm-trees.<br /> <br /> Are you laying siege to a city with mile high walls and a garrison of elite troops? Take the form of a bird, fly over the walls, then spend the next month living as a rat within their walls and only taking human form at midnight to summon another blood ape for your burgeoning army.<br /> <br /> Do you need to silently subvert a city against the Realm's plans? Steal the skin of its Satrap's favorite concubine and cast Peacock Shadow Eyes on him as you enter the room. Need a lock of somebody's hair or a drop of their blood for a working? Mice and mosquitos got you covered?<br /> <br /> Want to seed somebody's pockets with coins of distant vision? Seduce the Queen's tailor, steal his form, and sew one of the coins into the hem of the dress she will wear to the upcoming diplomatic meeting.<br /> <br /> Do you think that the Implosion Bow crew in your next battle is going to expect a mole to emerge from the ground, cast Impenetrable Darkness, and laugh as the Dragon-Blooded attuned to them burn excellencies trying to tear down and move their complicated machinery while their mortal crew routs?<br /> <br /> A Lunar sorcerer doesn't do sorcery in the best way possible, they do it the way you never saw coming. Yeah, Solars can achieve all these things through different means, but unless things have changed dramatically for shapeshifting, you, my hypothetical Lunar, can do them with your default powerset - No huge investment in Dexterity and Stealth and dive into other charm trees required.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the Silver Pact is totally going to have approaches to sorcery, shaping rituals, and workings that aren't in the core book. This is gonna probably be where you get into some of the extremely flavorful stuff. Also, that whole Wyld enhanced sorcery shaping ritual is a lot more useful when you have moonsilver tattoos and a tribe of beastfolk that already live in the Wyld anyway.<br /> <br /> All in all, there are a lot of ways being a Lunar Sorcerer could hypothetically encourage a style of play that is meaningfully different from being a Solar in ways that feed into themes of witchery and folkloric trickery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 08-12-2018, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}